<BaseLayout
  title="About — Settled"
  description="What Settled is, who runs it, and how we make picks."
>
  <h1>About Settled</h1>

  <p>
    Settled is a recommendations site for small-space kitchens. We test
    products that promise to make tight kitchens work — knife strips,
    drying racks, slim spice storage — and write up the ones that earn
    their counter or wall space.
  </p>

  <h2>How we pick</h2>
  <p>
    Each article lays out the criteria up front. Products that fail two
    or more criteria get cut. Among the survivors, we pick what we'd
    keep using a year in, not what has the loudest marketing.
  </p>

  <h2>How we make money</h2>
  <p>
    Articles include affiliate links, mostly to Amazon. If you click and
    buy, we may earn a small commission at no extra cost to you. We
    never accept payment to include a product, and we don't write about
    things we wouldn't keep ourselves.
  </p>

  <h2>What we don't do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Sponsored posts marked as editorial.</li>
    <li>"Best of" lists where we haven't actually tested the picks.</li>
    <li>Affiliate links to products we don't recommend.</li>
    <li>Pop-ups, autoplay video, or interstitials.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    See the <a href="/editorial-policy">editorial policy</a> for the full
    version.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
